{
  "header": [
    "PEERS — the peer set suite `py-prototype` declares it drives, as DATA. ADR-0003 §7.3 clause 1.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until 2026-09-16 the peer set was `KEYSTONE_PEERS ?= python rust go",
    "typescript` in the Makefile, overridden on the command line for the 33-peer and 37-peer runs. So",
    "the set that decided every number we have published was AN ARGUMENT SOMEONE HAPPENED TO TYPE, and",
    "no artifact recorded which one. AGENTS.md's fairness rule names that exact failure one level up —",
    "*an input that decides the outcome, chosen once, by one party, and never written down* — and the",
    "operator's direction was to apply it to the suite/peer axis too.",
    "",
    "⛔ WHAT THIS FILE MAY AND MAY NOT CONTAIN. It declares the SET, because choosing a set is OUR act.",
    "It declares NOTHING ABOUT ANY PEER — not its language, not its tier, not its spec pin, not whether",
    "it is certified. Those are keystone's facts and are read out of keystone's tree on every run",
    "(ADR-0003 §7.2, adopted from entity-system-generator's check-eligible.py: *'a copy of that",
    "vocabulary here is exactly the kind of fact AGENTS.md says we never keep. A declared name keystone",
    "does not define FAILS.'*). D16 is the same rule as a discipline, and it has already caught one",
    "live violation in this tree.",
    "",
    "⚠ MEMBERSHIP IS A RULE, NOT A LIST, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. `include` is `roster` — every peer on",
    "keystone's tools/peer-tiers.tsv — minus the exclusions below. Freezing 33 names here would have",
    "re-committed the original defect in a new file: a list goes stale silently as the cohort grows,",
    "and the cohort grew from 17 to 46 while a prose policy said 17."
  ],
