  "declared": "2026-09-16",
  "adr": "docs/adr/0003-a-requirement-is-not-a-probe.md §7",
  "rationale": [
    "Suite 1 drives the WIDEST set it can reach, and it is the only suite, so 'widest' is not a",
    "diversity claim — it is the absence of a choice. ⭐ THIS IS THE POINT WORTH BEING PRECISE ABOUT:",
    "a single suite over 37 peers is ONE INSTRUMENT'S REACH, not joint coverage, and a cohort all",
    "passing one author's checks is cohort-consistent rather than independently convergent",
    "(AGENTS-STANDARD, 'Never overclaim'). Breadth here buys peer-defect discovery. It buys NOTHING",
    "toward the question this repo exists to answer.",
    "",
    "⇒ So suite 1 takes the wide set, and ADR-0003 §7.3 clause 3 requires suite 2's declared set to be",
    "NEITHER IDENTICAL NOR NESTED in this one. Because this set is the roster, any suite-2 set is a",
    "subset of it, and `lint-peer-diversity` would refuse every possible declaration. ⛔ THAT IS A REAL",
