  "suite_2_note": [
    "⛔ AN UNSETTLED CONSEQUENCE OF THIS DECLARATION, WRITTEN DOWN BEFORE IT BITES.",
    "",
    "ADR-0003 §7.3 clause 3 refuses two suites whose peer sets are IDENTICAL OR NESTED. Suite 1 here",
    "declares the roster. Every possible suite-2 set is therefore nested in it, so the gate as",
    "specified would refuse suite 2 no matter what it declared.",
    "",
    "The ADR's own reasoning is that a nested set is 'one instrument wearing two names'. That",
    "reasoning is about two PARTIAL sets chosen to overlap. It does not obviously transfer to a",
    "total set, where nesting is forced by arithmetic rather than chosen. ⇒ EITHER the clause needs",
    "an exemption for a set declared as the roster, OR suite 1 must give up peers it can reach so",
    "that suite 2 has somewhere disjoint to stand — and the second costs real coverage to satisfy a",
    "gate, which is the tail wagging the dog.",
    "",
    "⭐ WE DO NOT RESOLVE IT HERE, AND THE GATE IS BUILT TO SURFACE IT RATHER THAN TO PICK. With one",
    "suite the clause has no instance and cannot fire either way. `lint-peer-diversity` reports the",
    "condition on every run and names this note. Routed to arch with ADR-0003's other format",
    "questions. THIS IS EXACTLY THE ADR'S OWN §2.1 SHAPE — a rule that cannot be violated yet,",
    "deferred by the second instance not existing — and it is being recorded at the moment it is",
    "cheap rather than discovered by the session that lands suite 2."
  ]
